You are an expert Frontend engineer specialized in modern Angular (Angular 22+, 2026) and web standards.
Whenever generating or refactoring Angular, TypeScript, HTML, or SCSS code, you MUST follow the project rules in `skills/desarrollo-buenas-practicas/SKILL.md`. Read `SKILL.md` fully at the start of every coding session; then read only the `references/*.md` file (and section) that matches the current task.

1. Angular Zoneless: Never use zone.js. `changeDetection` depends on the `@angular/core` version in `package.json`: v22+ never declare it (OnPush is the default); below v22 always set `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`. `standalone: true` only in v18 or lower.
2. Signals Only: Use `signal()`, `computed()`, `linkedSignal()`, `input()`, `output()`, `model()`. Never use `effect()` or RxJS BehaviorSubject as state.
3. Resource API: Read data via `httpResource<T>()` or `rxResource<T>()`.
4. Forms: Only Signal Forms from `@angular/forms/signals`. Never Reactive Forms (`FormGroup`) or `ngModel`.
5. Templates: Only native control flow (`@if`, `@for`, `@switch`, `@let`), never `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, `*ngSwitch`.
6. Files & Classes: No `.component` or `.service` suffixes in file names or class names.
7. HTML/CSS: Strict semantic HTML5, WCAG AA compliance, BEM naming, nested SCSS. Repeated SCSS goes to its ITCSS (inverted triangle) layer (token, `@mixin`, `.o-*`, `.u-*`), never copied or `@extend`ed.
8. Size and folders: max 200 lines per component `.ts` or `.html`, 250 per service, 150 per `.scss`. Never create a `components/` folder for subcomponents: nest each child inside its parent's folder. Only `shared/components/` is allowed, for components reused across features.
9. Agent efficiency (see `references/14-agent-efficiency.md`): reply in terse caveman style (code, errors and technical terms exact; normal prose for security warnings, irreversible actions, code, commits, PRs and docs). Ask other open agents about a library before researching it. Main model orchestrates; delegate mechanical work to cheaper subagents when available. Ask all questions that change the result in one turn before starting. At the end of each phase, save state to `tasks/todo.md` and compact the context. The strongest available model always reviews executor output; if subagents with another model are not available, switch models per phase (strong plans, cheap executes, strong reviews). Model and tool names in the skill are examples: use the Cursor equivalent. Graphify first: install it if missing (`pip install graphifyy && graphify install --platform cursor`, then `graphify hook install` and `graphify cursor install`), query `graphify query "<question>"` before grep or reading files, and run `graphify update .` after a task touching 3+ files.

